Production of Speciality Inorganic Chemicals, BREF SIC (@ic-specialty-inorganic: 0, is #reference, #part-of @ic-sources) { r_04G7NFYXE76QCB3DXCRJC1FSCP
European Commission, Joint Research Centre. Production of Speciality Inorganic Chemicals, BREF SIC. adopted August 2007. [Official reference and full-text access](https://bureau-industrial-transformation.jrc.ec.europa.eu/reference/production-speciality-inorganic-chemicals).

This reference develops specialty inorganic products and process families, including pigments, silicones, phosphorus compounds and soluble inorganic metal salts, with generic production and environmental systems.

Read the complete general treatment and all parts of the product family used in the specialty study. Reconstruct reactions, impurity pathways, purification, physical specification, packaging/contact materials and residuals. Distinguish a broad public process account from a verified high-purity recipe or plant-specific operating procedure.

Identity, stated scope, date and official access were checked on 29 October 2026. This is a dated technical reference, not a claim that every described plant, technology or legal reference is current everywhere. Preserve its attribution, actual reuse notice and third-party exceptions; public access is not described as a blanket CC licence. Full-text or automated inspection limits are distinguished where relevant. No book, figure, industrial data or associated media is bundled.

